# Node dependencies for scripts/agent (the only Node package here).
node_modules/

# Scratch space for the agent scripts' own tests. novelty.test.mjs creates
# throwaway git repositories under here and says it picks the location because
# it is ignored — an interrupted run otherwise leaves a nested .git that
# `git add -A` commits as a gitlink.
.harness-reports/

# The per-lane CI reports `scripts/ci/run-lanes.mjs` writes and `ci.yml`
# uploads for the CI-fix loop to read (docs/design/ci-lane-reports.md).
#
# A SECOND DIRECTORY, deliberately, and the one above is why. The name
# `.harness-reports/` is the one the upstream pipeline uses for exactly this
# artifact, and it was already taken here by something with incompatible
# contents: novelty.test.mjs plants whole git repositories under it. Sharing
# it would put a nested `.git` inside the upload's search root — @actions/glob
# walks it, and the artifact would carry throwaway repositories a local `node
# --test` run happened to leave behind, on a runner where the two would race
# for the same path. Renaming the scratch directory instead would have edited
# a test's isolation guarantee to make room for a reports sink, which is the
# wrong file to touch.
.ci-reports/

# Claude Code's per-user settings. It holds `permissions.allow` grants and the
# hook wiring `scripts/hooks/install.mjs` writes; committing one by accident
# both widens the permission set for every contributor and makes a branch able
# to run code on anyone who checks it out. There is deliberately no tracked
# .claude/settings.json to sit beside — see that installer's header.
.claude/settings.local.json
